1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:01,620
(Episode 2)

2
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:02,620
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

3
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:18,150
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

4
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:31,520
Oh, my.

5
00:00:35,947 --> 00:00:38,847
I'm sure we made eye contact.

6
00:00:40,817 --> 00:00:42,117
Did she not recognise me?

7
00:01:07,447 --> 00:01:08,777
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

8
00:01:08,777 --> 00:01:12,217
(Open)

9
00:01:20,717 --> 00:01:23,277
Why was he here?

10
00:01:30,747 --> 00:01:32,517
Did you get some sleep?

11
00:01:33,847 --> 00:01:35,147
You need to take your blood pressure medication.

12
00:01:38,917 --> 00:01:41,777
What is wrong with skipping it for one day?

13
00:01:42,217 --> 00:01:43,547
No.

14
00:01:44,117 --> 00:01:45,147
Hurry up and take it.

15
00:01:46,147 --> 00:01:47,947
Is this the only pill I take?

16
00:01:48,017 --> 00:01:51,017
You give me a whole pile of supplements.

17
00:01:51,077 --> 00:01:53,447
Are you trying to make me explode and die early?

18
00:01:55,417 --> 00:01:57,017
Of course not.

19
00:01:57,247 --> 00:01:59,917
I just want to live a long time with you.

20
00:02:00,517 --> 00:02:02,477
You know that, but you are still saying it.

21
00:02:02,547 --> 00:02:04,447
Open your mouth now.

22
00:02:06,947 --> 00:02:07,947
Ready!

23
00:02:09,247 --> 00:02:10,247
Here.

24
00:02:53,647 --> 00:02:54,747
Mom.

25
00:03:05,417 --> 00:03:06,717
I like it.

26
00:03:08,577 --> 00:03:10,517
Should I ask them to pick out a brooch for me?

27
00:03:18,247 --> 00:03:21,647
It has been a while, my dear niece. Have you been well?

28
00:03:21,947 --> 00:03:23,347
Are you eating well?

29
00:03:25,847 --> 00:03:27,417
(Delete)

30
00:03:41,617 --> 00:03:42,617
Manager Kang.

31
00:03:46,817 --> 00:03:47,947
Manager Kang.

32
00:03:49,377 --> 00:03:50,617
Manager Kang.

33
00:03:51,377 --> 00:03:53,047
Yes, ma'am.

34
00:03:59,177 --> 00:04:00,177
What do I do?

35
00:04:16,247 --> 00:04:17,447
It is okay.

36
00:04:18,017 --> 00:04:19,047
Just leave it.

37
00:04:20,377 --> 00:04:23,917
I'm so sorry. I made a mistake.

38
00:04:23,987 --> 00:04:26,317
I will take it to the store right away and have it cleaned...

39
00:04:26,917 --> 00:04:29,547
I'm going to throw it away anyway, so just leave it.

40
00:04:30,077 --> 00:04:31,877
No, but how can I do that?

41
00:04:32,277 --> 00:04:35,277
I know it costs over 30,000 dollars.

42
00:04:35,647 --> 00:04:37,817
If I press it with a towel like this,

43
00:04:37,877 --> 00:04:39,917
I think I can just treat the stain...

44
00:04:42,647 --> 00:04:44,117
I said I'm going to throw it away.

45
00:04:44,647 --> 00:04:46,177
Do you not understand what I'm saying?

46
00:04:47,977 --> 00:04:49,017
Throw it away right now.

47
00:04:51,147 --> 00:04:52,177
Ma'am.

48
00:04:52,447 --> 00:04:54,147
You are really pushing it.

49
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:01,817
Kang Da Mi.

50
00:05:02,547 --> 00:05:05,147
How on earth do you train your employees?

51
00:05:13,377 --> 00:05:14,477
Let go.

52
00:05:14,847 --> 00:05:16,217
I'm sorry, CEO Jeon.

53
00:05:16,517 --> 00:05:19,547
An unfortunate incident occurred while I was away for a moment.

54
00:05:20,247 --> 00:05:21,247
For the bag,

55
00:05:21,247 --> 00:05:23,077
according to the department store's VIP policy,

56
00:05:23,077 --> 00:05:25,077
after reporting the situation to the department in charge,

57
00:05:25,147 --> 00:05:27,347
we will compensate you accordingly.

58
00:05:28,177 --> 00:05:30,877
However, please apologize to my colleague.

59
00:05:32,177 --> 00:05:33,647
For using violence against her.

60
00:05:37,477 --> 00:05:38,977
You want me to apologize?

61
00:05:39,347 --> 00:05:40,547
Yes.

62
00:05:41,177 --> 00:05:42,177
Da Mi.

63
00:05:44,947 --> 00:05:46,217
Manager Kang.

64
00:05:46,747 --> 00:05:48,117
Do you not care about tomorrow?

65
00:05:49,217 --> 00:05:51,517
Yes, I suppose so.

66
00:05:54,377 --> 00:05:55,377
CEO Jeon?

67
00:06:00,017 --> 00:06:02,377
- Hi, Team Leader Cha. - I was looking around the stores,

68
00:06:02,447 --> 00:06:03,877
and stopped by because I heard you were here.

69
00:06:08,017 --> 00:06:09,217
What is going on?

70
00:06:09,617 --> 00:06:10,647
Well...

71
00:06:10,917 --> 00:06:13,647
Oh, there is no need to panic, Manager Kang.

72
00:06:14,117 --> 00:06:16,717
It is my fault for carelessly spilling the juice.

73
00:06:18,277 --> 00:06:20,147
But why was she...

74
00:06:20,917 --> 00:06:21,917
holding your arm?

75
00:06:22,917 --> 00:06:24,247
She was trying...

76
00:06:26,017 --> 00:06:28,447
to pick up the broken glass with her hands,

77
00:06:28,517 --> 00:06:30,917
so I was just stopping her from doing that.

78
00:06:31,447 --> 00:06:33,117
I was worried she might get hurt.

79
00:06:34,317 --> 00:06:35,377
That is right, Team Leader Cha.

80
00:06:36,577 --> 00:06:38,977
I will go change my clothes, so wait a moment.

81
00:06:39,377 --> 00:06:41,847
Since we are both here, let us look around together.

82
00:06:55,447 --> 00:06:56,447
Take this.

83
00:07:01,917 --> 00:07:04,017
No, I'm fine.

84
00:07:18,947 --> 00:07:19,947
Let's go.

85
00:07:22,477 --> 00:07:23,477
Keep up the good work.

86
00:07:27,247 --> 00:07:28,747
Goodbye, CEO Jeon.

87
00:07:34,717 --> 00:07:36,447
Did you see that, Da Mi?

88
00:07:36,517 --> 00:07:38,777
How could she change her attitude so quickly?

89
00:07:39,747 --> 00:07:41,847
Anyway, thank you, Da Mi.

90
00:07:42,247 --> 00:07:43,547
Are you okay where she hit you?

91
00:07:44,677 --> 00:07:47,217
Oh my goodness, it is swollen.

92
00:07:47,447 --> 00:07:49,877
- Will it be okay? - We have an ice pack, right?

93
00:07:49,947 --> 00:07:52,717
Go ice it right away. You need to get the swelling down quickly.

94
00:07:52,947 --> 00:07:56,517
No, not my face. I mean the bag.

95
00:07:56,587 --> 00:07:58,147
It is really expensive.

96
00:07:58,647 --> 00:08:00,217
You are more precious.

97
00:08:00,277 --> 00:08:02,317
More than that bag worth tens of thousands of dollars.

98
00:08:02,377 --> 00:08:04,777
More than all the luxury goods here combined.

99
00:08:05,147 --> 00:08:06,147
Do you understand?

100
00:08:08,647 --> 00:08:10,277
If she files a complaint,

101
00:08:10,347 --> 00:08:12,377
I will take responsibility, so do not worry.

102
00:08:20,717 --> 00:08:22,947
(50 dollars)

103
00:08:42,917 --> 00:08:44,947
Let's just eat by ourselves.

104
00:08:48,517 --> 00:08:49,747
What's going on?

105
00:08:50,217 --> 00:08:52,547
Has no one arrived yet?

106
00:08:53,017 --> 00:08:54,587
That is strange.

107
00:08:54,947 --> 00:08:57,817
Su Ah's mom is not answering her phone at all.

108
00:08:57,877 --> 00:08:59,877
I have not been able to reach her since this afternoon.

109
00:09:00,217 --> 00:09:03,047
She is probably busy or took Su Ah to the hospital.

110
00:09:03,117 --> 00:09:07,347
They are unbelievable. They can forget a lot of things,

111
00:09:07,417 --> 00:09:08,547
but their mother's birthday?

112
00:09:10,617 --> 00:09:12,917
I mean, the daughter-in-law is disappointing,

113
00:09:12,977 --> 00:09:16,087
but how can all three children be exactly the same?

114
00:09:16,477 --> 00:09:19,547
And it is past time for Da Mi to get off work too.

115
00:09:20,117 --> 00:09:21,147
Please eat, Mother.

116
00:09:22,417 --> 00:09:23,747
Oh my goodness.

117
00:09:24,117 --> 00:09:26,847
It feels like I'm having my 60th birthday feast early.

118
00:09:27,477 --> 00:09:30,317
- Thank you. - What do I always tell you?

119
00:09:30,847 --> 00:09:33,617
If you just keep your children under your wing...

120
00:09:33,647 --> 00:09:35,377
and spoil them...

121
00:09:35,447 --> 00:09:37,247
You brought this on yourself, Mi Mi.

122
00:09:37,317 --> 00:09:40,247
You spoiled and coddled your kids after your husband left.

123
00:09:40,317 --> 00:09:43,047
I knew from then on that you would end up like this someday.

124
00:09:45,447 --> 00:09:46,517
That is enough.

125
00:09:49,747 --> 00:09:51,777
There is no need to walk on eggshells around me.

126
00:09:52,777 --> 00:09:55,117
They do not even show their faces on their own mother's birthday.

127
00:09:55,177 --> 00:09:57,347
Those ungrateful brats deserve a good beating,

128
00:09:57,417 --> 00:09:59,377
so why should you walk on eggshells?

129
00:10:05,347 --> 00:10:06,647
(Terminal 1)

130
00:10:17,977 --> 00:10:22,447
(Taxi Stand)

131
00:10:22,517 --> 00:10:24,147
(Available)

132
00:10:25,147 --> 00:10:26,217
Oh, hello.

133
00:10:52,717 --> 00:10:54,777
Are you coming back from a business trip?

134
00:10:55,947 --> 00:10:57,447
No, I have returned for good.

135
00:10:57,517 --> 00:10:58,617
Oh, I see.

136
00:11:00,747 --> 00:11:03,047
It really took a long time.

137
00:11:03,577 --> 00:11:04,577
Excuse me?

138
00:11:05,677 --> 00:11:07,047
I mean, it really took a long time to come back.

139
00:11:23,747 --> 00:11:24,977
Excuse me, sir.

140
00:11:25,317 --> 00:11:26,947
You only said Seoul,

141
00:11:27,017 --> 00:11:29,877
but you have not given me an exact destination yet.

142
00:11:30,247 --> 00:11:32,517
So, are you heading home?

143
00:11:34,347 --> 00:11:35,347
Well...

144
00:11:36,947 --> 00:11:39,077
Please take me to the Gold K Hotel.

145
00:11:39,217 --> 00:11:40,677
Yes, understood.

146
00:11:40,917 --> 00:11:41,947
Thank you.

147
00:12:06,277 --> 00:12:07,277
Here.

148
00:12:10,447 --> 00:12:12,817
Oh my gosh, what's going on here? Grandma!

149
00:12:16,017 --> 00:12:17,677
These are all my mom's clothes.

150
00:12:18,077 --> 00:12:21,117
Grandma, do you know how much these cost?

151
00:12:24,017 --> 00:12:25,577
- Grandma. - What?

152
00:12:25,647 --> 00:12:28,377
You were doing so well all day, why are you acting like this again?

153
00:12:28,447 --> 00:12:31,177
These are for my sons,

154
00:12:31,247 --> 00:12:34,077
fabric for Jun Sung and In Sung's clothes.

155
00:12:34,377 --> 00:12:38,147
Oh, give that here. I need to stuff them with cotton...

156
00:12:38,217 --> 00:12:40,547
and make pants for them. Give it to me now.

157
00:12:40,617 --> 00:12:42,677
Come on, Grandma.

158
00:12:42,747 --> 00:12:45,047
Uncle Jun Sung passed away a long time ago,

159
00:12:45,117 --> 00:12:46,947
and my dad has plenty of nice clothes.

160
00:12:47,317 --> 00:12:49,677
Your family is super rich now. Do you not remember?

161
00:12:49,977 --> 00:12:51,077
What?

162
00:12:53,647 --> 00:12:56,977
Oh, tell them to go buy a cheesecake.

163
00:12:57,047 --> 00:12:59,517
- A cheesecake. - A cheesecake?

164
00:12:59,847 --> 00:13:02,647
- At this time of night? - My eldest son, Jun Sung,

165
00:13:02,747 --> 00:13:07,247
- likes that the most. - Okay, Grandma.

166
00:13:07,317 --> 00:13:09,417
I will ask Do Yun to buy one.

167
00:13:09,477 --> 00:13:14,277
No, not Do Yun. Tell Seung Yun to buy it.

168
00:13:14,917 --> 00:13:17,547
Oh, call Seung Yun quickly.

169
00:13:17,847 --> 00:13:20,677
How is Seung Yun supposed to buy it when he is in the US?

170
00:13:20,747 --> 00:13:22,077
And I just called him a little while ago.

171
00:13:22,147 --> 00:13:23,377
His phone is turned off.

172
00:13:24,147 --> 00:13:25,847
He must be busy preparing to return home.

173
00:13:36,317 --> 00:13:38,377
- Do Yun, hello. - Hello, I'm on my way home, why?

174
00:13:40,147 --> 00:13:42,217
- Thank you. Have a good night. - Thank you.

175
00:13:43,247 --> 00:13:46,217
Oh, thank goodness. I will have one cheesecake, please.

176
00:13:46,277 --> 00:13:47,277
Sure.

177
00:13:55,347 --> 00:13:57,777
Do you need candles? How many should I put in?

178
00:13:57,847 --> 00:13:58,847
Well...

179
00:14:00,177 --> 00:14:01,617
No candles, thank you.

180
00:14:01,647 --> 00:14:03,917
Okay, I will buy it and be right home.

181
00:14:04,217 --> 00:14:05,647
Take good care of Grandma.

182
00:14:05,647 --> 00:14:06,717
Okay.

183
00:14:09,247 --> 00:14:11,817
My mom would be embarrassed if I put candles on it.

184
00:14:11,877 --> 00:14:14,347
- Do you have any cheesecake left? - Oh, I'm sorry, sir.

185
00:14:14,417 --> 00:14:17,047
The one this customer just bought was the last one.

186
00:14:17,117 --> 00:14:18,917
Oh, thank you. Have a good night.

187
00:14:20,077 --> 00:14:21,317
Excuse me.

188
00:14:21,877 --> 00:14:22,877
Oh my goodness.

189
00:14:22,947 --> 00:14:25,377
You are the department store staff from earlier today, right?

190
00:14:27,277 --> 00:14:30,377
I'm sorry, but could I buy this cake from you?

191
00:14:30,777 --> 00:14:31,777
Excuse me?

192
00:14:31,847 --> 00:14:33,877
I'm in a hurry and just bought this myself.

193
00:14:33,947 --> 00:14:36,577
I really need it right now.

194
00:14:36,647 --> 00:14:38,417
I bought it because I really need it today, too.

195
00:14:38,477 --> 00:14:40,647
Oh, all the other cakes here are delicious, too.

196
00:14:40,747 --> 00:14:42,017
I will buy you as many as you want.

197
00:14:43,517 --> 00:14:46,077
For now, please give this one to me.

198
00:14:47,517 --> 00:14:48,517
No.

199
00:14:52,847 --> 00:14:54,577
Hey, wait a minute.

200
00:14:56,647 --> 00:14:57,647
Oh my.

201
00:15:00,317 --> 00:15:01,317
Darn it.

202
00:15:04,477 --> 00:15:05,477
Darn...

203
00:15:09,577 --> 00:15:10,847
I'm sorry.

204
00:15:11,317 --> 00:15:12,617
What should I do about this?

205
00:15:19,777 --> 00:15:20,777
Excuse me.

206
00:15:25,747 --> 00:15:26,847
Please take this.

207
00:15:27,347 --> 00:15:29,717
It is ruined anyway, so please let me have it.

208
00:15:33,217 --> 00:15:34,847
I said no, so why do you keep doing this?

209
00:15:35,447 --> 00:15:36,477
You did this earlier too,

210
00:15:36,547 --> 00:15:38,077
and you think money solves everything?

211
00:15:45,777 --> 00:15:48,077
- What is this? - What does it look like?

212
00:15:48,147 --> 00:15:50,147
It is what you left behind earlier today.

213
00:15:57,447 --> 00:15:59,277
You said you were a team leader at Hwanggeum Apparel, right?

214
00:15:59,747 --> 00:16:01,747
I don't know how much you make as a team leader,

215
00:16:01,817 --> 00:16:03,247
but you tried to solve things with money earlier today,

216
00:16:03,317 --> 00:16:05,417
and you are still so desperate to throw money at me now?

217
00:16:05,817 --> 00:16:07,677
I really like money too,

218
00:16:07,877 --> 00:16:10,017
but I really do not want to take yours.

219
00:16:10,347 --> 00:16:11,517
Earlier today, my mo...

220
00:16:12,947 --> 00:16:15,717
Did you have some other problem with CEO Jeon?

221
00:16:17,747 --> 00:16:21,947
If you are really that curious, you should ask your boss directly.

222
00:16:42,377 --> 00:16:43,417
- I'm home. - Hey.

223
00:16:43,417 --> 00:16:44,547
You are late, my son.

224
00:16:45,347 --> 00:16:46,547
Do Yun, you are empty-handed?

225
00:16:47,747 --> 00:16:49,447
Yes, they were all sold out.

226
00:16:50,547 --> 00:16:51,847
Is Grandma still looking for it?

227
00:16:52,217 --> 00:16:53,417
Do not worry.

228
00:16:53,477 --> 00:16:55,217
She fell asleep right after taking her medicine.

229
00:16:55,877 --> 00:16:58,347
Do Yun, are you not hungry? Should I make you something to eat?

230
00:16:58,417 --> 00:17:01,017
No, I'm fine. I will go to my room and rest.

231
00:17:04,817 --> 00:17:05,947
By the way, Mom.

232
00:17:06,447 --> 00:17:07,477
Yes.

233
00:17:07,717 --> 00:17:09,847
About earlier today at the department store...

234
00:17:11,217 --> 00:17:12,477
What about the department store?

235
00:17:14,917 --> 00:17:19,117
If you are really that curious, you should ask your boss directly.

236
00:17:21,747 --> 00:17:22,747
Never mind.

237
00:17:27,577 --> 00:17:29,017
Did something happen earlier today?

238
00:17:30,447 --> 00:17:33,317
Nothing happened. I was just a little tired,

239
00:17:33,377 --> 00:17:34,947
and Do Yun must have been worried about me.

240
00:17:36,117 --> 00:17:40,217
He is exactly like Dad in that way. He is so sweet to Mom.

241
00:17:41,447 --> 00:17:43,077
Do Yun might be sweet,

242
00:17:43,147 --> 00:17:45,677
but he has a long way to go to match your dad, Se Na.

243
00:17:46,377 --> 00:17:48,377
I love hearing that compliment, honey.

244
00:17:50,977 --> 00:17:52,077
Hey, Se Na.

245
00:17:52,147 --> 00:17:54,317
How long are you going to just stay at home?

246
00:17:54,377 --> 00:17:55,377
Prepare to study abroad...

247
00:17:55,377 --> 00:17:56,447
if you do not want to retake the college entrance exam.

248
00:17:56,917 --> 00:17:59,177
I keep telling you I have no interest in studying.

249
00:17:59,717 --> 00:18:01,447
I'm going to start my own business.

250
00:18:01,917 --> 00:18:04,017
Hey, even if you start a business,

251
00:18:04,017 --> 00:18:06,247
you should at least get a college degree first.

252
00:18:06,247 --> 00:18:08,617
By the way, when did you say Seung Yun is coming back?

253
00:18:08,977 --> 00:18:11,247
Well... I talked to him earlier today,

254
00:18:11,317 --> 00:18:12,847
and he said he will come back within this week.

255
00:18:13,147 --> 00:18:15,787
It has been years since my oldest brother came back.

256
00:18:16,317 --> 00:18:17,477
I can't wait to see him.

257
00:18:19,417 --> 00:18:21,617
To have such a good relationship between cousins,

258
00:18:21,677 --> 00:18:23,817
you really raised the kids well.

259
00:18:24,517 --> 00:18:25,647
To Seung Yun, we are...

260
00:18:25,717 --> 00:18:28,447
taking the place of your late brother and his wife.

261
00:18:29,147 --> 00:18:31,287
I consider Seung Yun to be my own child.

262
00:18:35,177 --> 00:18:36,617
(Aunt)

263
00:18:41,717 --> 00:18:42,917
Why are you not answering?

264
00:18:44,877 --> 00:18:46,447
I will take it in the room.

265
00:18:46,717 --> 00:18:48,917
A friend said she had something to discuss earlier.

266
00:19:07,347 --> 00:19:09,047
Should I go to the office tomorrow?

267
00:19:09,117 --> 00:19:10,147
She's crazy.

268
00:19:17,947 --> 00:19:19,447
I will call you back in a little bit.

269
00:19:33,117 --> 00:19:35,847
I should have just given it to him when he asked nicely.

270
00:19:38,647 --> 00:19:40,447
Earlier today, my mo...

271
00:19:40,517 --> 00:19:43,447
Did you have some other problem with CEO Jeon?

272
00:19:43,517 --> 00:19:47,617
If you are really that curious, you should ask your boss directly.

273
00:19:48,787 --> 00:19:50,817
You should have held back a little, Kang Da Mi.

274
00:19:50,877 --> 00:19:52,877
Why did you do that?

275
00:19:52,947 --> 00:19:55,577
If that team leader or whoever actually asks,

276
00:19:55,647 --> 00:19:57,447
and the CEO of Hwanggeum Apparel finds out...

277
00:19:58,547 --> 00:20:01,647
And if she files a complaint and I end up getting fired...

278
00:20:11,577 --> 00:20:12,977
Why did you not just come home tomorrow?

279
00:20:14,317 --> 00:20:16,647
Did Mi Seon really not come?

280
00:20:16,717 --> 00:20:18,117
She did not.

281
00:20:18,787 --> 00:20:20,447
My brothers must have come, right?

282
00:20:22,017 --> 00:20:25,117
Neither Kang Gang Nam nor Kang Dae Chi came.

283
00:20:25,177 --> 00:20:26,787
Your mother is just walking on eggshells around her mother-in-law,

284
00:20:26,847 --> 00:20:27,917
so she is not saying anything,

285
00:20:27,977 --> 00:20:29,787
but imagine how upset she must have been.

286
00:20:29,847 --> 00:20:30,947
What are you going to do?

287
00:20:31,787 --> 00:20:33,647
I'm sorry, Aunt Ri Ja.

288
00:20:34,377 --> 00:20:35,647
It is the first time this has happened,

289
00:20:35,647 --> 00:20:36,747
so please let it slide.

290
00:20:36,747 --> 00:20:38,287
You were not like this when you were young.

291
00:20:38,347 --> 00:20:40,717
How can you become so selfish as you get older?

292
00:20:40,787 --> 00:20:43,147
Gang Nam and Dae Chi need to treat her well, too,

293
00:20:43,217 --> 00:20:46,647
but you really need to be good to your mother.

294
00:20:46,717 --> 00:20:47,717
You know that, right?

295
00:20:51,877 --> 00:20:53,077
Are you upset?

296
00:20:54,747 --> 00:20:55,747
Yes, Aunt Ri Ja.

297
00:20:56,747 --> 00:20:59,447
Whenever I'm about to forget, you throw that in my face.

298
00:20:59,977 --> 00:21:02,047
It upsets me, and it hurts.

299
00:21:03,517 --> 00:21:05,747
I'm sorry for being so blunt,

300
00:21:05,747 --> 00:21:08,377
but my one and only older sister sometimes seems like...

301
00:21:08,447 --> 00:21:10,647
the most pitiful person in the world to me.

302
00:21:10,747 --> 00:21:12,147
I feel bad for her.

303
00:21:13,017 --> 00:21:14,277
When you get married...

304
00:21:14,347 --> 00:21:16,077
and have kids of your own, you will understand.

305
00:21:17,547 --> 00:21:19,117
I will pay more attention to Mom.

306
00:21:22,117 --> 00:21:23,547
Oh, my.

307
00:21:24,877 --> 00:21:27,117
They say if you take in another's child,

308
00:21:27,177 --> 00:21:29,477
it will pay off someday, but look at this.

309
00:21:29,477 --> 00:21:31,277
Darn it, seriously.

310
00:21:32,677 --> 00:21:33,677
Unbelievable.

311
00:21:40,077 --> 00:21:41,377
This is so distracting.

312
00:21:43,377 --> 00:21:45,617
She only knows how to make a mess.

313
00:21:46,177 --> 00:21:48,647
If I don't clean it for even one day, it turns into a pigsty.

314
00:22:12,077 --> 00:22:13,217
Wait.

315
00:22:13,747 --> 00:22:15,277
How does she have this?

316
00:22:19,647 --> 00:22:20,717
Mom, what are you doing?

317
00:22:22,077 --> 00:22:23,547
Oh, you are home?

318
00:22:25,017 --> 00:22:28,017
I was just trying to tidy up...

319
00:22:28,017 --> 00:22:30,447
I told you not to clean my room.

320
00:22:30,517 --> 00:22:32,647
Why are you opening someone else's drawers?

321
00:22:34,117 --> 00:22:35,417
Oh my, Da Mi.

322
00:22:36,417 --> 00:22:38,147
Don't talk like we are not strangers.

323
00:22:38,647 --> 00:22:40,147
A mother can try to clean her daughter's room...

324
00:22:40,217 --> 00:22:41,417
and accidentally see things, right?

325
00:22:43,917 --> 00:22:45,077
Anyway, I'm sorry.

326
00:22:45,677 --> 00:22:46,977
I will never touch your room again.

327
00:22:48,547 --> 00:22:50,147
I'm sorry for getting mad, Mom.

328
00:22:51,347 --> 00:22:53,317
I didn't even celebrate your birthday today.

329
00:22:54,647 --> 00:22:55,647
But...

330
00:22:58,617 --> 00:23:00,347
When I think about you,

331
00:23:01,077 --> 00:23:02,177
I know I should...

332
00:23:02,247 --> 00:23:03,917
really hate the dad who abandoned us,

333
00:23:04,247 --> 00:23:05,717
and I really do hate him.

334
00:23:08,947 --> 00:23:10,217
It is okay, tell me.

335
00:23:13,177 --> 00:23:16,077
I still wanted to keep a few photos of him.

336
00:23:17,077 --> 00:23:18,747
We only lived together for a few years,

337
00:23:19,717 --> 00:23:22,377
but he was still my dad for a little while.

338
00:23:22,947 --> 00:23:25,017
The dad who raised me is still my dad.

339
00:23:27,117 --> 00:23:29,377
But when I think about what he did to you,

340
00:23:29,447 --> 00:23:31,017
I know I should not do this.

341
00:23:31,447 --> 00:23:33,677
I'm sorry. I will throw them away.

342
00:23:34,317 --> 00:23:36,047
Your grandmother still has it too.

343
00:23:37,317 --> 00:23:38,977
I'm fine. You don't have to throw them away.

344
00:23:40,047 --> 00:23:41,177
Hurry up and wash up for bed.

345
00:23:42,647 --> 00:23:44,777
I left a cheesecake in the kitchen.

346
00:23:45,217 --> 00:23:47,347
It is a bit squished because I dropped it on the way.

347
00:23:49,147 --> 00:23:50,217
Got it.

348
00:24:06,547 --> 00:24:09,877
But why are Gang Nam and Dae Chi not here yet?

349
00:24:29,177 --> 00:24:31,147
Did she fall while bringing this home?

350
00:24:32,447 --> 00:24:33,917
Did she get hurt?

351
00:24:35,247 --> 00:24:39,247
Oh, please. I saw her come in, and she was perfectly fine.

352
00:24:39,317 --> 00:24:41,517
Stop worrying so much about your grown daughter.

353
00:24:43,317 --> 00:24:44,577
This looks delicious.

354
00:24:47,777 --> 00:24:52,077
- I thought you were on a diet. - Diets always start tomorrow.

355
00:24:53,617 --> 00:24:56,247
Hey. You know elders eat first.

356
00:24:59,617 --> 00:25:00,647
Hand it over.

357
00:25:04,047 --> 00:25:06,177
9 times 8 is 72.

358
00:25:06,647 --> 00:25:09,577
9 times 7 is 63.

359
00:25:11,177 --> 00:25:14,817
9 times 6 is 54, and 9 times five is...

360
00:25:15,717 --> 00:25:17,147
Let me see...

361
00:25:17,577 --> 00:25:19,047
Is it 46?

362
00:25:19,047 --> 00:25:20,117
Right?

363
00:25:21,617 --> 00:25:22,877
It is 45.

364
00:25:24,647 --> 00:25:27,477
Have a bite. Da Mi bought it.

365
00:25:28,647 --> 00:25:31,277
She might not be very affectionate,

366
00:25:31,347 --> 00:25:35,777
but either way, Da Mi is the best out of the three.

367
00:25:36,847 --> 00:25:39,377
You did a good thing taking her in back then.

368
00:25:41,747 --> 00:25:44,417
Do you really think so, Mother?

369
00:25:47,047 --> 00:25:48,217
Where was I?

370
00:25:49,547 --> 00:25:51,647
9 times 5 is 45.

371
00:25:52,247 --> 00:25:54,717
Soon Deok, it is 45.

372
00:25:56,147 --> 00:25:57,447
9 times 4 is...

373
00:25:59,347 --> 00:26:00,777
A narrow escape from death.

374
00:26:28,917 --> 00:26:30,477
My age this year.

375
00:26:33,017 --> 00:26:35,717
I will be 60 before I know it.

376
00:26:38,147 --> 00:26:41,017
I still wanted to keep a few photos of him.

377
00:26:42,047 --> 00:26:43,877
We only lived together for a few years,

378
00:26:44,877 --> 00:26:47,377
but he was still my dad for a little while.

379
00:26:47,847 --> 00:26:50,317
The dad who raised me is still my dad.

380
00:26:50,647 --> 00:26:53,647
She might not be very affectionate.

381
00:26:53,717 --> 00:26:56,217
You did a good thing taking her in back then.

382
00:26:58,517 --> 00:27:00,077
It was more than just a good thing.

383
00:27:01,547 --> 00:27:03,447
She saved my life, Mother.

384
00:27:05,947 --> 00:27:07,717
If I had not met Da Mi that day,

385
00:27:09,117 --> 00:27:10,917
I would not be in this world anymore.

386
00:27:27,577 --> 00:27:30,447
(Mission: Mompossible)

387
00:27:30,747 --> 00:27:31,947
What a strange woman.

388
00:27:32,017 --> 00:27:34,017
I mean, I apologised when I first met her,

389
00:27:34,077 --> 00:27:35,477
and tried to pay her back. That should have been enough.

390
00:27:35,547 --> 00:27:38,377
What more could I do? What exactly did I do wrong?

391
00:27:38,617 --> 00:27:40,917
Who is calling at this hour of the night?

392
00:27:40,977 --> 00:27:42,047
"Jeon Jin Sook?"

393
00:27:42,117 --> 00:27:44,917
Is Jeon Jin Sook someone from your company?

394
00:27:45,117 --> 00:27:46,247
Mi Seon.

395
00:27:47,347 --> 00:27:48,617
Su Ah's mom.

396
00:27:48,877 --> 00:27:50,647
They moved out a few days ago.

397
00:27:50,647 --> 00:27:52,547
Ma'am, did you not know?

398
00:27:52,617 --> 00:27:55,577
They moved out? My son and his wife?

399
00:28:03,477 --> 00:28:04,877
(Mission: Mompossible)
